__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# `uv run` writes this, and it is deliberately not committed. It pins a *dev*
# environment and nothing reads it at build time: the image installs with `pip`
# from the source tree, so a committed lock here would look like the
# reproducibility fix the image needs and would not be it. That fix is a
# constraints file beside the packaging, and it is P9-I53's rather than this
# task's to take.
uv.lock
